### A* Algorithm
A* is a best-first search algorithm that uses both the cost of the path from the start node to the current node (`g(n)`), and an estimate of the cost of the path from the current node to the goal (`h(n)`). The total cost of a path from the start node to the goal node is `f(n) = g(n) + h(n)`. The heuristic used should be admissible (never overestimates the cost) and consistent (for any given node `n`, every neighboring node `m` has `h(m) <= h(n) + d(n, m)`).

